+| Power-limited CPU: how fast the frame's bottleneck threads (GPU back and front, Vulkan worker, guest cores) really run, on which cores, and what spinning or the power mode costs | `EDEN_NX2_CLOCK_TRACE=1` (Windows; read on first use, so `nx2_switches.txt` works too) | One `Clock trace (EDEN_NX2_CLOCK_TRACE):` line after the first second: the core classes (P, E, LP-E: the SoC tile's island) with their logical processors, `EfficiencyClass` and nominal MHz (and which classes' nominal clock is not the TSC rate: check those classes' `ghz` against HWiNFO's core clocks once), the power plan, the power mode (Settings > Power) and the user-configured one where Windows has it, AC, battery saver and battery, the plan's base AC values (boost mode, maximum and minimum processor state, energy performance preference, the `EfficiencyClass 1` ones too; the power mode may change them), the package power counters found, the TSC rate and what one read of the processor counters costs. Every 10 s a `Clock trace per second` line (`HW.GPU`): per role group (`back`, `front`, `vulkan_worker`, `guest_cores`, `busiest_guest_core`: the guest core with the most work) `ghz` (the CPU-time-weighted effective clock of the processors it ran on: Processor Frequency times % Processor Performance, from PDH each second), `cpu_ms` (CPU ms per second), `poll_ms` (its polls before it sleeps: the back's and front's spin for each other, a guest core's idle poll; Windows counts them as running) and `work_ms` (`cpu_ms` minus `poll_ms`), its share on `p`, `e` and `lpe` cores and `migrations` per second (a lower bound that includes wake-ups on another core); per core class `busy` (mean % Processor Time), `util` (% Processor Utility: busy times clock over base, above 100% in turbo) and `ghz` (busy-weighted), with each P-core as `GHz@busy`, fastest first; `power` per Energy Meter (RAPL) or Power Meter instance in W, or `n/a`; `power_mode`, `user_mode`, `ac`, `battery_saver`, `battery` (charge, `charging`) and whether they `changed`; then `trace overhead`, the sampler thread's own CPU ms per second (not the hooks' calls on the role threads). `ghz` averages in whatever else ran on those cores, polls included, and leaves out halted time, so it reads above HWiNFO's effective clock; `cpu_ms` and `gpu_back_cpu_ms_per_frame` include the polls, so judge a change by frame times first, then by the back's `work_ms` and the P-cores' `ghz` at equal package power. Kernel lock and address-wait spins (`EDEN_NX2_KSPIN`, `EDEN_NX2_ARB_SPIN`) count as work; a thread's time since the last 10 ms sample goes to the processor it published last, so `migrations` also says how far to trust its shares. Other hosts log `Clock trace: not supported on this host` at each game start. |
 | Shader stutter or not, boot and cache costs | `EDEN_NX2_STUTTER_TRACE=1` | One `Nx2Stutter` line per frame presented over 33 ms after the last, with its top cause (gfx/compute pipeline built on the GPU thread, pipeline wait, shader capture, texture, buffer, query/fence, present, other) and each GPU thread's ms; `Nx2StutterSummary` every 10 s (frame-time histogram, builds, cache lookups, cache file size); `Nx2Boot` boot phases with commit and peak commit. Frames over `EDEN_NX2_STUTTER_DETAIL_MS` (default 50) also get `Nx2StutterDetail`: each GPU thread's eight largest zones (ms/calls) and the rare sites that ran (device memory allocate/free, staging, buffer and image create/delete/GC, synchronous downloads, `Scheduler::Finish`), with each run over 2 ms by thread; the summary adds the sites per 10 s. The category totals in the summary are every frame's steady cost, not hitch time. `python3 -I tools/nx2/cache_metrics.py parse <log>` turns a log into JSON, `compare` A/B runs; `tools/nx2/cache_bench.py` runs the cold/warm matrix on the PC. |
 | Command corruption or pop-in | `EDEN_NX2_PB_CHECK=1`; A/B with `EDEN_NX2_PB_SNAPSHOT=0` or `EDEN_NX2_FETCH_DRAIN=1` | How many pushbuffer entries change between submit and parse. |
 | Commands read from memory instead of their submit-time copy (frames ahead, #392) | `EDEN_NX2_LIVE_READ_CHECK=1` | Every 10000 such entries, `Entries parsed from memory (<reason>): N checked, M differ` per reason, plus the first four differing entries per reason. GPU-written pages differ by design (the GPU rewrote them after submit), so compare against a frames-ahead-0 run. |
@@ -94,6 +95,7 @@ Use these before guessing. All are off unless the variable is set; pass them as
 | Wrong macro parameters read by DMA on the split's front | `EDEN_NX2_DMA_READ_VERIFY=1` | A macro DMA read made without draining the split drains it anyway and is compared. Every 10 s a `Macro DMA read checks` line: reads, those made without a drain and those that read other words than after a drain (must stay 0), with the first 16 differing reads. |
 | Upscaler and DLSS contracts | `EDEN_NX2_DLSS_CONTRACT_TRACE=1` | Inputs and outputs of replaced upscaler networks. |
 | Service calls | `EDEN_NX2_IPC_TRACE=1` | IPC command trace. |
+| Guest heap map/unmap cost (frame rates that differ by session in one area, slow `MapPhysicalMemory` in the guest core lines) | `EDEN_NX2_HEAP_TRACE=1`, in the environment (read at startup, not from `nx2_switches.txt`) | Every 10 s a `MapPhysicalMemory per second` and an `UnmapPhysicalMemory per second` line (`HW.Memory`): calls, MiB asked for and MiB that changed, total ms, p50/p99/max µs per call (from before the physical memory lock), and ms per part: lock wait, allocation, zero fill (MiB and GB/s), page table, host map or unmap (with the host regions per call), the unmapped pages' freeing, other, then the trace's own overhead, which the call times leave out. On Windows also the MiB the maps committed (`EDEN_NX2_SEC_RESERVE`) and page faults during the calls (per call and per second; the process's, so other threads' faults in that time count too), then the process's faults per second, working set and commit, and the host's available RAM and commit charge. |
 | Read stalls (loading hitches, NUP vs other containers) | `EDEN_NX2_FS_READ_TRACE=1` | About once a second while the guest reads, one `Guest storage reads` line (`IStorage`, the RomFS) and one `Guest file reads` line (`IFile`): count, MiB, p50/p99/max latency and reads over 1 ms and 16 ms, plus totals and read time since boot. Times cover the backend read (NUP decompression included), not the Switch 1 SD-card throttle. |
 | Unmapped device reads (`Unmapped Device ReadBlock`) | `EDEN_NX2_READBLOCK_TRACE=1` | Every read of unmapped device memory, one line per read with its first unmapped address, unmapped byte count and caller (`file:line`). Without it only the first 16 are logged. |
 | Device loss (`Device loss occurred!`) | Always on | The `Device fault` lines after it: what VK_EXT_device_fault reports (fault addresses and their type, vendor fault codes). `not supported by the driver` means the driver has no such data. |
